  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="We&apos;ll Be Back!" id="e957-8c69-1203-279c" hidden="false">
      <comment>Updated rule in Chapture Approved 2004</comment>
      <description>Any model with the Necron special rule that is reduced to 0 wounds, or would otherwise be removed as a casualty, is instead laid on its side to show that it&apos;s damaged. At the start of every Necron turn, damaged Necrons with 6&quot; of a model of the same type may self-repair. On a roll of 1-3, remove the model as normal. On a 4-6, the Necron is repaired and stands back up with 1 Wound remaining and joins the closest unit of the same type. 
A model cannot self-repair if it was destroyed by a close combat weapon that allows no Armour saves or any weapon whose Strength is twice the Toughness of the Necron. Models destroyed due to a failed &apos;Death or Glory&apos; attack may not be repaired by any means.
Necron Lords do have need to have another model with 6&quot; in order to self-repair.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Phase Out" id="d2b0-ba08-4fb1-d9f3" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Necron army is reduced to 25% or less of its original number of models with the Necron special ability. it will disappear in an eerie fasion, leaving behind nothing of its presence. This gives an automatic victory to the enemy, regardless of the victory conditions of the scenario being played. Do not include C&apos;tan, Pariahs, Scarab Swarms, Monoliths and Tomb Spiders towards the number of destroyed models or the total original size of the army.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warscythe" id="671a-44a9-6e39-0b7b" hidden="false">
      <description>There are no saving throws of any sort (including invulnerable saves) allowed against Warscythes, and when attacking vehicles 2D6 + Strength is rolled for armor penetration.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Terrifying Visage" id="3dd1-2c47-6416-fd3e" hidden="false">
      <description>Units in close combat with this unit must take a Leadership test at the start of each round of combat. If they fail then for that round they may only hit this unit on a roll of 6 regardless of WS. Models that either need not take model tests or which are assumed to automatically pass them are unaffected by this rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immune to Natural Law" id="dd4a-0561-881b-06c7" hidden="false">
      <description>C&apos;tan are able to warp reality around them to varying degrees. C&apos;tan ignore terrain when moving, will tend to float above impassable terrain and cannot claim to be &quot;inside&quot; objects to avoid being shot at. When attacking models in or behind cover, C&apos;tan count as having frag grenades so will strike simultaneously.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Necrodermis" id="5f9e-1076-dc6d-0047" hidden="false">
      <description>C&apos;tan have a Invulnerable save of 4+. If it loses all of its wounds, the nexrodermis is breached and the essence of the C&apos;tan is released. This inflicts a S6 hit on every model within D6&quot; of the C&apos;tan with no Armor Save possible.
If a Wraithcannon inflicts instant death on a C&apos;tan it will not be transported to the warp but will take a wound without the benefit of its Invulnerable Saving throw. If a C&apos;tan phase sword or knife strikes a C&apos;tan it will inflict no wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drain Life" id="768f-1e22-adae-e966" hidden="false">
      <description>A C&apos;tan&apos;s close combat attacks drain the life energy from its opponents. Any model reduced to 0 Wounds by a C&apos;tan will not regenerate or recover because of bionics, nartheciums, exsanguinators, or any other similar wargear.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Manifestation" id="b49f-9537-ab4f-f2bb" hidden="false">
      <description>The C&apos;tan is a living god. Any unit that wishes to assault the C&apos;tan must take a Leadership test. If the test if failed, the unit&apos;s nerve crascks in the face of ageless evil and it may not make an assault that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Above All Others" id="05c1-c9ef-2f06-46e7" hidden="false">
      <description>C&apos;tan may not join friendly units and may be picked out by enemy shooters even if within 6&quot; of other targets.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Disruption Field" id="c7a0-c570-c859-6963" hidden="false">
      <description>Disruption Fields are used in assaults against vehicles. Any hit inflicted on a target by a unit equipped with disruption fields will score a glancing hit on a D6 roll of 6 regardless of the vehicles Armor value in exactly the same manner as gauss weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gauss Weapons" id="ec1e-b09d-90d9-bba3" hidden="false">
      <description>Against troops, any roll to would of a 6 automatically causes a would regardless of Toughness. Agaisnt vehicles, any roll of 6 will cause a glancing hit if it does not already cause a penetrating hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Living Metal" id="7952-d645-54f2-4e49" hidden="false">
      <description>Attacks which count the target&apos;s Armor Value as being less than it really is do not do so against the Monolith. Similarly, weapons that get additional Armor Penetration dice do not get the extra dice against the Monolith. Ordnance weapons still roll 2D6 and select the highest.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tesla" id="6f5b-5593-89e2-7728" hidden="false">
      <comment>7th Edition Rule seems most fair and in line with 3rd edition type play</comment>
      <description>A Tesla weapon that rolls a to hit of a 6 causes 2 hits on a target instead of only 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shroud" id="c4ab-4235-0b02-127d" hidden="false">
      <description>A Shourd system wreaths the Necron vehicle in a shifting miasma of impenetrable shadow. All shooting attacks made against the vehicle use the night fighting special rule if it is not already in use.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
