        <modifier field="4d99-7daa-b467-798a" type="set" value="0">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="7a63-eaa2-fd49-2b4e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Gaze of Death" id="6f28-cb4c-cd42-6143" hidden="false">
          <description>The Nightbringer may choose to use the Gaze of Death instead of attacking normally in close combat. Place the Ordnance template over the C&apos;tan. Any enemy models entirely beneath it are hit automatically. models partially beneath it are hit on a D6 roll of 4+. Every model hit takes a Strength 4 hit with no Armor Saving throw permitted.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Etheric Tempest" id="2201-5dd1-be8d-3399" hidden="false">
          <description>In the beginning of the enemy Assault phase, after moves have been made but before any blows are struck, the Nightbringer may harness its power to summon etheric winds which hurl its opponents away from it. Any enemy unit (not vehicles) with a model within 6&quot; and which doesn&apos;t consist entirely of models with unmodified Strength 4 or more must move 2D6&quot; directly away from Nightbringer as if it was failling back.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Night Scythe (Homebrew)" id="f851-9166-e134-2d28" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <comment>7th Ed rules and VDR (ignoring some of restrictions put in place for Necrons by CA2004)

Flyer-Normal
Armor - 11-11-11 = 5+30+20=55
Flyer=40

Living Metal=50
Tesla Destructor=50 (based on some analysis this appears to be worth 50 points compared to any autocannon after considering Tesla)</comment>
